  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Institutional capacity and competence to implement maritime policies, standards and regulations improved.</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2018">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">Align the existing maritime legislation with EU requirements</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Develop the programmatic fiches based on the Blue Economy Programme for Albania. 
- Gather feedback and reflect comments from national stakeholders and line ministries on the programmatic project fiches.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">The respective programmatic project fiches based on the Blue Economy Programme were developed following a participatory approach and in consultation and cooperation with line Ministries in charge, and the Unit for Development Programs and Cooperation in the Department for Development and Good governance in the Prime Minister&#x2019;s Office. This progrmme is in line with the EU Blue Economy Report 2021. 

The project fiches areas of focus are (i) Tourism and innovation ( ii) fishery and aquaculture ( iii) Industry and port development</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">-Technical expertise to support in achieving compliance with EU Regulations, Directives and International Conventions.
-Training Needs Assessment (TNA)
-Training of the trainers (ToT)
- A national Blue Economy Programme
-Integrated solutions and awareness raised for maritime and environmental pollution.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x2022;	An addition of 13 EU Directives and Regulations as well as international Maritime Organisation (IMO)&#x2019;s guidelines, and the tables of concordances were developed in compliance with EU requirements. 
&#x2022;	A series of meetings organized 9-10 September 2020 with the Steering Committee, representing the Ministry of Infrastructure and Energy (MIE), General Maritime Directorate (GMD) and other stakeholders. During this meeting, the training needs and areas of development for the Maritime sector according to the organisational priorities of GMD and MIE were assessed. 
&#x2022;	Training Needs Assessments finalized.
&#x2022;	Training of Trainers modules developed and Trainings and Masterclasses conducted. 
&#x2022;	National Blue Economy Programme developed.
&#x2022;	Report on assessment and recommendations for the implementation of IMO AP and MARPOL Annex 5 .
&#x2022;	Report on in inland water transport assessment for Albania 
&#x2022;	Trainings of the Safety and Security maritime staff on effective application of the institutional capacity building in the field of Maritime Safety and Security in line with the Paris Memorandum of Understanding (Paris MoU);</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">-Integrated solutions and awareness raised for maritime and environmental pollution.
-Capacity building of national stakeholders for the Blue Economy Programme</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
    </period>
   </indicator>
